# Royal Road (`RoyalRoad/`)

- Id `royalroad`, book ids `rr:*`. Never change either; they key users' books, data and sign-in.
- The plugin parses site HTML, so a site markup change shows up as an empty list or a PARSE error.
  Keep the markup probes (`markupProbe`, `describeHtml`) and `flow.log` lines: they are how a
  broken page is diagnosed from the app's Plugins debug channel.
- Chapter body is `div.chapter-inner` only. Author notes are the `authorNotes` setting (default off,
  compared with `=== true`).
- Follow, Favorite and Read Later are `syncable` lists; the app's two-way sync calls
  `setMembership`, `syncProgress` and `readPositions`. Keep their contracts in
  `../flow-reader/docs/plugins/api-functions.md`.
- Add a parsing test with a trimmed fixture in `test/royalroad.test.mjs` for every markup fix;
  `test/fixtures-raw/` is git-ignored, so commit only small, scrubbed fixtures inline.
- Release: bump `version` in `plugin.json`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, commit `index.json`.
